<title>SINGAPORE: Lion Teck Chiang debuts at IPO price.</title>
<headline>Lion Teck Chiang debuts at IPO price.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in property and steel company Lion Teck Chiang Ltd opened their first day of trading in Singapore on Thursday at Singapore $1.30 each, unchanged from their initial public offer (IPO) price.  </p>
<p>Lion Teck Chiang, a member of Malaysian conglomerate The Lion Group, had offered 32.52 million shares, of which 18.1 million were available to the public.</p>
<p>The public offer tranche was 2.9 times subscribed but only 78 percent of its restricted offer, to existing shareholders, was taken up, the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>By 0110 GMT, the shares stood at S$1.33.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
